{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #90: declared status 'disproved'. Formalized: yes. Does every set of $n$ distinct points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ contain at most $n^{1+O(1/\\log\\log n)}$ many pairs which are distance 1 apart? Current best: In \\cite{Er82e} he offers \\$300 for the upper bound $n^{1+o(1)}$. This would be the best possible, as is shown by a set of lattice points. The best known upper bound is $O(n^{4/3})$, due to Spencer, Szemer\\'{e}di, and Trotter \\cite{SST84}. In \\cite{Er83c} and \\cite{Er85} Erd\\H{o}s offers \\$250 for an upper bound of the form $n^{1+o(1)}$. Prize: $500. OEIS: A186705. Tags: distances, geometry."},"claim_id":"vcl_5fbae09e29c1f8ea9e25b170ea58698b71bb35cabe313c6f92f0205a5c46ef0d","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:90","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_a713c4f009cbe7ed","object_root":"sha256:5356187d500a4f3be5b29880db931aa69c3275a5d00a9589a50b31fc1e898f18","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_recor